WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.560
It's been a very long night.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:08.469
It is the first day after the 20 20 presidential
Senate and House election and unfortunately,

00:00:08.469 --> 00:00:14.860
we really don't have that many results yet,
at least not enough to say who will be the

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.430
president of the United States for the next
four years.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.640
And it's really difficult to do these shows
because things move so quickly and then nothing

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.550
happens for hours and things move quickly.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:29.730
And because it takes us about 90 minutes to
produce the show, I try in the interests of

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:35.360
getting you all the most updated and accurate
information on which we can then go to the

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.260
next day.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.971
It becomes tough to know exactly when to do
the show, but at a certain point we have to

00:00:41.971 --> 00:00:44.059
do it and we're doing it right now.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:49.440
So I will give you the information that is
accurate as of this moment, some of this may

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.440
have changed.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.819
And if so, at our next opportunity to be together,
we will discuss it.

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:57.410
There is not yet a winner in the 2020 presidential
election.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.059
I will look at specific numbers with you in
a little bit.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:03.800
But as of this morning, the Associated Press
had it.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.830
Two hundred and thirty eight electoral votes
for Joseph R. Biden Jr., the Democratic candidate,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:14.720
and 213 electoral votes for Donald Trump.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.720
And yet Donald Trump declared victory late
last night, early this morning.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.570
I will have clips of that for you.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.180
That is exactly as I predicted.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.240
But the most important reminder I have, and
this was starting to become an issue on last

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.610
night's dream.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.580
We anticipated this scenario.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:40.870
We had over one and a half million different
people, including nearly 100000 at a time,

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:46.170
watched the live stream of the results last
night and panic was rapidly rising.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.040
I had people in Europe calling.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.970
It was 4:00 or 5:00 in the morning there.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.560
They were up all night watching the numbers.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.180
We have to remember the Red Mirage scenario
now.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.620
Trump may win.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.840
Biden may win.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:05.210
This was an election because we knew that
there were going to be postal delays partially

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.090
caused by the president's postmaster general.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:11.950
There are now 300000 potentially missing ballots,
which I will tell you about.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:15.069
I will tell you all of what is going on.

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:21.290
Some states which count in person and report
in-person ballots first and then start counting

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.790
the mail in ballots.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:27.560
We knew of a potential red meraj scenario
where states would look like they were going

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.560
Trump.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.400
And as the ballots are counted, they start
looking towards Biden.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.219
We already have two examples of this.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.819
Wisconsin and Michigan.

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:39.900
They are not final numbers yet, but Wisconsin
and Michigan all night yesterday, even until

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.900
midnight.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.959
And later, we're looking like, wow, Trump's
crushing Michigan.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:50.450
And slowly but surely, the numbers have shifted
and are now leaning in favor of Joseph R.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.450
Biden Jr..

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.810
So panic does not serve us well in these situations.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.470
We don't think clearly when we're panicking.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.889
And importantly, we're panicking over things
we can't control.

00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:08.540
If we learn about ballots being thrown out,
then, yes, we activate and we start calling

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.280
the people who need to be called and complaining
and making a lot of noise, but merely waiting

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.890
for ballots to be counted when we anticipated
a Red Mirage scenario doesn't serve us well.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:23.629
And in fact, as I tweeted last night around
twelve thirty in the morning, remember how

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:29.439
we were warned about a red meraj and not to
panic at midnight on Tuesday?

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:31.049
I'm going to bed.

00:03:31.049 --> 00:03:33.999
Many vote counts don't even resume until the
morning.

00:03:33.999 --> 00:03:36.189
And indeed, that's what I did.

00:03:36.189 --> 00:03:40.909
And indeed, as the vote counts have resumed,
the numbers have started to shift in Joe Biden's

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:43.040
favor in a number of states.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.739
I'm speaking generally now.

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:47.040
I will get to specifics in the next segment.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:52.819
Now, as a quick reminder, in the midst of
all of this, remember, we still have a pandemic.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:55.920
We had another nearly 100000 cases yesterday.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.560
And on top of all of the normal delays that
can sometimes happen on top of the delays

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.219
that we're aware of in the mail, on top of
all of these other things, most states are

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:10.930
also being relatively safe when it comes to
the pandemic in terms of elections staff and

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.719
counting and all of these things.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:16.530
So let's not forget about that reality as
we discussed the election results.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.209
So momentarily we're going to do a deep dove
into the presidential map.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:24.600
In terms of the Senate, we still don't know
who will control the Senate right now.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:30.020
Democrats have flipped two seats, John Hickenlooper,
one in Colorado, and Mark Kelly defeating

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:36.440
the incumbent Republican vile Republican Martha
McSally in Arizona.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.960
Republicans have also flipped one seat.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.460
We expected that Democratic Senator Doug Jones
would lose in Alabama and he did.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:48.169
So that's Democrats plus two Republicans plus
one.

00:04:48.169 --> 00:04:51.819
That is one seat in the direction of Democrats
so far.

00:04:51.819 --> 00:04:58.259
Otherwise, counting continues in the House
of Representatives, votes still being counted

00:04:58.259 --> 00:04:59.259
as of one.

00:04:59.259 --> 00:05:03.979
A moment earlier today, Democrats securing
one hundred and ninety seats, flipping to

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:10.220
firm Republicans, Republicans securing one
hundred and eighty one, flipping six, meaning

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:16.510
a net gain of four for Republicans with 64
seats remaining to count.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:23.139
I'm going to take some time to go through
the presidential numbers in a moment.

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:25.620
This is going to take some time.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.780
As long as we're confident in the votes being
counted, it doesn't bother me, although I

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.530
understand it is stressful and anxiety producing.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.940
The problem we're up against is Donald Trump
is trying to end the election.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.539
Now, Donald Trump has declared victory.

00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:45.940
Donald Trump declared that he won states,
which it's not actually clear that he won.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:50.190
And we know of hundreds of thousands of votes
that are potentially missing.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:06:10.009
And we're going to cover 

00:06:10.009 --> 00:06:35.870
all of 

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:51.599
it 

00:06:51.599 --> 00:07:16.080
for you today.

